    "result": "`encode` and `decode` are now implemented in `solution.py` according to `spec.md`, and `python -m pytest -q tests` passes with 20 tests. I did not run a coverage report, so the 90% line-coverage gate is unconfirmed.\n\nThe tests in `tests/test_solution.py` check:\n- **Encoding:** runs of 4 or more, runs of `~`, and long runs.\n- **Round trips:** `decode(encode(s))` returns `s`.\n- **Lenient decoding:** well-formed text that `encode` wouldn't produce, such as plain `\"aaaa\"`.\n- **Error cases:** each case the spec says should raise `ValueError`.\n\nOne fragile spot: the leading-zero check in `decode` has a redundant condition. It still rejects every case I tried.",
